    "evidence_text": "Coordination of Rho GTPase activities during cell protrusion\n\nThese data suggest treatment strategies that target RAS/RAC pathways and ROS production in human MDS/AML.\n\nLeukemias and other cancers possess self-renewing stem cells that help to maintain the cancer.\n\nSurprisingly, activation of LARG and GEF-H1 involves distinct signalling pathways.\n\nIn addition, large deletions are found in NHEJ products exclusively in BCR/ABL cells.\n\nTo address these questions, we established an assay for GTP-bound cellular Rho.\n\nThe activation phase was greatly enhanced by serum.\n\nFurthermore, suspended cells showed higher Rho activity than adherent cells in the presence of serum.\n\nThese data indicate the existence of an adhesion-dependent negative-feedback loop.\n\nOur results show that ECM, cytoskeletal structures and soluble factors all contribute to regulation of Rho activity.\n\nRedox-dependent downregulation of Rho by Rac\n\nRole of RhoA-specific guanine exchange factors in regulation of endomitosis in megakaryocytes.\n\nRho, Rac and Cdc42 regulate actin organization and cell adhesion in macrophages.\n\nThese results demonstrate that Src activation contributes to pancreatic tumor progression in this model, offering Src as a candidate for targeted therapy.",
